WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.203
With thirty-three elements and thirty-two
threads per block, main launches two

00:00:05.203 --> 00:00:05.660
blocks.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.066
Each thread needs to work out which array
index belongs to it.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.374
CUDA grid of one returns the index across
all blocks.

00:00:14.554 --> 00:00:18.629
Multiply the block number by the threads
per block and add the thread number.

00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:22.385
Block one, thread zero gets index
thirty-two.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:26.439
Index thirty-two is the last valid
position.

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:30.496
The next thread gets thirty-three and skips
the read and write.

00:00:30.676 --> 00:00:35.343
In the thread inspector, compare thread
zero and thread one of block one.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.655
Now select sixteen threads per block.

00:00:38.835 --> 00:00:42.435
Block two, thread zero writes the same
array position.

00:00:42.615 --> 00:00:46.539
Use last traced writer in the console
comparison to check it.
